Now the sequence is correct:
- pin(true [prompt, ster1]) ✓
- unpin ster1 when ster2 arrives... wait — order: pin(false [77bdb6b0]) THEN pin(true [93adb079]) ✓ — release before pin ✓
- then trailing pin(false [93adb079]) ×2 — release events after the final pin — from post-run flush cycles (releasing the already-pinned ids). Harmless but noisy: after the run ends, extra flush cycles re-release the SAME ids. pinnedSteringRecordIds should CLEAR after the release fires (the release is "take" semantics). Let me fix: after takeForFlush returns release, set pinnedSteringRecordIds = const [] unless new pins replaced it. Currently: `final release = pinnedSteringRecordIds;` then only replaced if steeringPin non-empty. So the release fires EVERY subsequent cycle. Fix: clear it:

```dart
final release = pinnedSteringRecordIds;
if (steringPin.isNotEmpty) {
