`_liveIndex`: find the live message matching by identity first, then by user-text equality. Deduplicate (the same pinned message may also be the carried turn — the turn is carried separately! If pinned == the newest real user turn... the turn re-homes via `caried`. If the pinned message IS the turn → carried twice → duplicate. Dedup: skip pinned whose index == turn index.)

Count dropped: `cut - summaries - carriedMail - pinnedCaried - (caried?1:0)`.

Order of re-home: summaries, marker, carriedMail, pinnedCaried, turn? The pinned task prompt should render EARLY (it's the assignment) — but the marker must precede the re-homed set. I'll place pinnedCaried right after carriedMail and before the turn.

